# The documents every dump1090 field name and column position in this
# package comes from (CLAUDE.md rule 8, LESSONS E-03), each at a pinned
# commit with the SHA-256 of the file as fetched from
# raw.githubusercontent.com. scripts/check-contracts.sh fetches each and
# fails on a different hash. A bump is a `build:` commit of its own, with
# the golden tests re-derived from the new document.
#
# aircraft.json: README-json.md, section "aircraft.json", names every key
# read here (now, aircraft, hex, type, flight, alt_baro, alt_geom, gs,
# track, baro_rate, geom_rate, squawk, emergency, lat, lon, nic, rc,
# seen_pos, version, nic_baro, nac_p, nac_v, sil, sil_type, gva, sda,
# mlat, tisb, seen) with its unit. Two facts it does not state are taken
# from the writer, generateAircraftJson in net_io.c at the same commit:
# alt_baro is the string "ground" for an aircraft on the ground (line
# 1769), and emergency is one of none, general, lifeguard, minfuel,
# nordo, unlawful, downed, reserved (emergency_enum_string, line 1673).
#
# SBS / BaseStation (port 30003): the repository has no prose description
# of this output. The authority is its writer, modesSendSBSOutput in
# net_io.c (lines 571-787), whose comments number the 22 columns
# ("Fields 1 to 6", "Fields 7 & 8", ... "Field 22"); this package reads
# exactly those positions. ASSUMPTIONS, marked where they are used: (1)
# the columns carry no unit, so the units are README-json.md's for the
# same quantities (altitude feet, ground speed knots, vertical rate
# feet/minute); (2) an altitude or vertical rate with the suffix "H" is
# the geometric quantity (written from altitude_geom / geom_rate when
# --gnss is set, "Show altitudes as HAE/GNSS when available", dump1090.c
# line 334), referenced to the WGS84 ellipsoid as README-json.md defines
# alt_geom; (3) columns 7-10 are the receiver's local time
# (localtime_r), so the zone is configuration (ANSP_ADAPTER_SBS_TIMEZONE);
# (4) the heartbeat is an empty line every 60 s by default
# (send_sbs_heartbeat; MODES_NET_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL in dump1090.h).
#
# <sha256> <owner/repo> <commit> <path in that repo>
